From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:02:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] present lock-on-lid as a three-state combo, and move
 the lid button down

Two dialog refinements the copyright holder asked for on seeing the
settings in place.

Lock on lid close was two checkboxes -- "Lock screen on lid close" and
"... even when docked" -- which between them can express a fourth,
meaningless combination: lock when docked but not otherwise. The states
that make sense are three, so it is a combobox now: Do not lock / Lock,
unless docked / Lock, even when docked. It still writes the same two
booleans the daemon reads (lockOnLidClose and lockOnLidCloseWhenDocked),
mapped so the nonsense state cannot be produced, and the lock-method combo
enables on any value that locks.

And the Lid close button moves to the bottom of the Button Events list,
below Power, Suspend and Suspend-to-disk. It is a switch rather than a
button and now sits next to the "Perform the lid-close action, even when
docked" checkbox that qualifies it, which is where a tester looked for the
relationship.

Both verified by rendering the generated dialog on each page.
